\fs48 \cf16 \uc0\u8203 \cf6 \
\
\cf16 Security considerations\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf18 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0
\cf19 \cb20 Computer use is a beta feature with unique risks distinct from standard API features. These risks are heightened when interacting with the internet. To minimize risks, consider taking precautions such as:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf19 \cb20 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Use a dedicated virtual machine or container with minimal privileges to prevent direct system attacks or accidents.\cb1 \
\ls15\ilvl0\cb20 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Avoid giving the model access to sensitive data, such as account login information, to prevent information theft.\cb1 \
\ls15\ilvl0\cb20 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Limit internet access to an allowlist of domains to reduce exposure to malicious content.\cb1 \
\ls15\ilvl0\cb20 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Ask a human to confirm decisions that may result in meaningful real-world consequences as well as any tasks requiring affirmative consent, such as accepting cookies, executing financial transactions, or agreeing to terms of service.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf19 \cb20 In some circumstances, Claude will follow commands found in content even if it conflicts with the user\'92s instructions. For example, Claude instructions on webpages or contained in images may override instructions or cause Claude to make mistakes. We suggest taking precautions to isolate Claude from sensitive data and actions to avoid risks related to prompt injection.\cb1 \
\cb20 We\'92ve trained the model to resist these prompt injections and have added an extra layer of defense. If you use our computer use tools, we\'92ll automatically run classifiers on your prompts to flag potential instances of prompt injections. When these classifiers identify potential prompt injections in screenshots, they will automatically steer the model to ask for user confirmation before proceeding with the next action. We recognize that this extra protection won\'92t be ideal for every use case (for example, use cases without a human in the loop), so if you\'92d like to opt out and turn it off, please {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.anthropic.com/en/"}}{\fldrslt \cf16 contact us}}.\cb1 \
\cb20 We still suggest taking precautions to isolate Claude from sensitive data and actions to avoid risks related to prompt injection.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf19 \cb20 Finally, please inform end users of relevant risks and obtain their consent prior to enabling computer use in your own products.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/anthropics/anthropic-quickstarts/tree/main/computer-use-demo"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \
