\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf5 When one of the Anthropic-defined tools is requested via the Anthropic API, a computer use-specific system prompt is generated. It\'92s similar to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/tool-use/implement-tool-use#tool-use-system-prompt"}}{\fldrslt \cf16 tool use system prompt}} but starts with:\
You have access to a set of functions you can use to answer the user\'92s question. This includes access to a sandboxed computing environment. You do NOT currently have the ability to inspect files or interact with external resources, except by invoking the below functions.\
As with regular tool use, the user-provided 
\fs28 \cf16 \cb17 system_prompt
\fs32 \cf5 \cb1  field is still respected and used in the construction of the combined system prompt.\
