\
\cf16 Enable thinking capability in Claude 4 and Claude Sonnet 3.7\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf5 Claude Sonnet 3.7 introduced a new \'93thinking\'94 capability that allows you to see the model\'92s reasoning process as it works through complex tasks. This feature helps you understand how Claude is approaching a problem and can be particularly valuable for debugging or educational purposes.\
To enable thinking, add a 
\fs28 \cf16 \cb17 thinking
\fs32 \cf5 \cb1  parameter to your API request:\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf26 \cb27 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf9 \cb8 Copy\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf36 \cb25 "thinking"\cf29 :\cf26  \cf30 \{\cf26 \
  \cf36 "type"\cf29 :\cf26  \cf31 "enabled"\cf30 ,\cf26 \
  \cf36 "budget_tokens"\cf29 :\cf26  \cf33 1024\cf26 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf30 \}\cf26 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf5 \cb1 The 
\fs28 \cf16 \cb17 budget_tokens
\fs32 \cf5 \cb1  parameter specifies how many tokens Claude can use for thinking. This is subtracted from your overall 
\fs28 \cf16 \cb17 max_tokens
\fs32 \cf5 \cb1  budget.\
When thinking is enabled, Claude will return its reasoning process as part of the response, which can help you:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls27\ilvl0\cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
